course: dictionary
lesson: 6781
title: Oracle: a word with a long history
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word oracle is one of them. In the old stories of Greece and Rome, an oracle was a priest or priestess who gave advice from the gods, or the holy place where this happened, like the Oracle of Delphi. Today, people also use oracle for someone who knows a lot. Context helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: «Shang kings, over 3,000 years ago, asked their ancestors questions by heating bones and shells until they cracked.» These oracle bones were not people. The clues are bones, shells and cracks, so here an oracle means a way of asking for answers from the past.
explain: «Ask Sam, he is the oracle for all things about dinosaurs.» Sam is not a priest, and nobody is asking the gods. The clue is that Sam knows a lot, so an oracle here means a person who knows everything about a subject.
fact: An oracle was a priest or priestess who people believed passed on messages from the gods.
fact: «Oracle» also means the holy place where the gods' advice was given, such as the Oracle of Delphi.
fact: «Oracle bones» are bones used in ancient China to ask questions, and they hold some of the oldest Chinese writing known.
fact: In everyday talk, a person who knows a lot about a subject can be called an oracle, which is an informal use.
fact: Context clues, like the words around the word, help you tell which meaning of a word is being used.
exercise: «Shang kings heated bones until they cracked and read the cracks as answers.» What were these bones used for? | To build houses | To make soup for dinner | To make music | *To ask questions and look for answers from the ancestors
exercise: «Greeks travelled to the Oracle at Delphi to ask questions.» What is the Oracle at Delphi? | A large ship | A river in Greece | *A holy place where people asked the gods for advice | A shop that sold pottery
exercise: Ella says, «Ask Sam, he is the oracle for all things about dinosaurs.» What does oracle mean here? | A dinosaur bone | A type of hat | A loud noise | *A person who knows a lot and gives advice
test:«The Oracle of Delphi often gave answers that were riddles.» What does this suggest about the answers? | They were written in English | They were always very short and clear | *They were puzzling, so people had to think hard | They were sung loudly
test:«These oracle bones hold the oldest Chinese writing known.» What can you learn from this sentence? | Oracle bones were made in Greece | *Oracle bones are among the oldest Chinese writing ever found | Oracle bones are modern computers | Oracle bones are only used for dinner plates
exam: What does the second meaning of oracle say? | A holy river | *A message or answer given by such an oracle | A type of bone only | A pair of shoes
